title: 'What it cost: the high notes of Jeff''s I was sent to read gave names, not claims.'
pid: 9f65a0e9-f5bd-427d-a182-e449037be0f0
body: |2-
  His "information" and "communication" drew 134 and 104 lines, his
  skg note 344, and most of their children were links titled with a
  topic ("art", "magic", "empathy"). I followed none. What told me
  what skg is for was Tay's list of Jeff's sentences from 'docs/',
  each a claim with its file. So the case reached me through a reader
  who had distilled it, which is what skg says it allows: to learn
  from another without either having to teach. Why the names failed me
  is in [[id:8910393c-e7f6-4f29-9d64-6cd3a26eba85][A link's words are all a reader has to decide whether to follow it]].
